package api

// Regression tests for request-body reading at POST /events:
//   - the 1 MiB body limit is enforced on raw UTF-8 bytes: 1048575 and
//     1048576-byte bodies are accepted, 1048577 bytes are rejected with
//     400 invalid_audit_input even when the extra byte is legal trailing
//     whitespace, and multi-byte characters (direct Chinese, supplementary
//     plane characters, \uXXXX escapes) count by bytes, not runes;
//   - a transport-level read failure is the same 400 invalid_audit_input
//     whether it happens before any data, mid-document, or after a complete
//     valid object (even one carrying an existing seq — the read failure
//     wins over the 409 conflict), and never persists the event;
//   - failed requests consume no sequence number and move no chain tail,
//     the database holds only successful requests, and a close/reopen keeps
//     records and tail intact while /healthz stays 200.
//
// All expectations go through the public HTTP entry and the persisted rows;
// hashes are recomputed from the public SHA-256 rule in README.md.
